<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tian Du</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 206 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian">Tian</a> Du was a general of Qi who joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>'s campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> and in 206 BCE was made King of Qi, with his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linzi">Linzi</a>, when Xiang Yu divided the old State of Qi into three kingdoms. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-rong">Tian Rong</a>, the clan strongman left out of the settlement, drove him out within months and reunited Qi under himself.</p></div>
